Sealed offline ARM64; GCC 14.2.0-19 and Clang 19.1.7, each O0/O2:
  cc -std=gnu11 -O{0,2} -c probe.c -o probe.o
  readelf -SW probe.o; readelf -sW probe.o
  gcc-14 -no-pie probe.o -o probe; ./probe
EvoCC assembly is assembled/linked by the same gcc-14.

                 boot_function    boot_data     execution
GCC14 O0/O2      .init.text       .init.data    0 / 0
Clang19 O0/O2    .init.text       .init.data    0 / 0
EvoCC            .text            .init.data    0

The function's section appears on a preceding declaration, so the expected
placement requires merged symbol attributes, not an emitter-only heuristic.
All five object compilations succeed. A returning-zero control does not
validate section placement or post-init lifetime behavior.

The active kernel's modpost.log has 2515 section-mismatch records and
372 distinct referring function names. These are relocation-warning counts,
not 2515 failed units, nor proof that every warning has this same cause.
