Current EvoIR 10.1.9 explicitly preserves unapplied section attributes;
Appendix D only authorizes explicit OBJECT sections. Function has no section
field, and native emission selects ordinary text. Full function-section
semantics have been requested for approval; no warning suppression, validator
relaxation, specification change, or active-kernel replacement was made.

2026-09-21 local time: original-object confirmation after final link failed.
Run 20260920T103126Z has CALL26 overflows from head.o .idmap.text to:

symbol                    reference section/size    subject section/size
__pi_create_init_idmap     .init.text / 212 bytes    .text / 2124 bytes
__pi_early_map_kernel      .init.text / 1164 bytes   .text / 1588 bytes

Both are GLOBAL FUNC. Source map_range.c:91 and map_kernel.c:241 declare
them __init; include/linux/init.h:45 maps it to section(".init.text").
The unchanged linker script separately places ordinary text, identity-map
code and init text. This is an observed section violation at the two actual
overflow targets, not proof that applying sections alone closes all linking.

