with exit 0; C-HIR and EvoIR interpreters each return 0.
function-section-boundaries.out records declaration-order, alias, static
label, always-inline, alignment and patchable-entry controls.

Six ORIGINAL .o.cmd records replayed with the existing actual generated
headers, not pristine headers; no object was installed by this targeted run.
All six assemble and have no missing/extra reference global symbols:
  arch/arm64/kernel/pi/map_range.o     4.850 s
  arch/arm64/kernel/pi/map_kernel.o    2.268 s
  security/landlock/syscalls.o        10.321 s
  security/landlock/ruleset.o          9.289 s
  net/ipv6/icmp.o                     8.690 s
  init/main.o                       10.353 s
Sealed readelf observes create_init_idmap and early_map_kernel in .init.text,
sizes 2124 and 1588 bytes, respectively (before Kbuild's __pi symbol prefix).
start_kernel is in .init.text; .ref.text is separate. Both code sections have
the required alignment. The three Landlock/ICMP objects have zero undefined
__compiletime_assert_* references. This establishes defined-name parity, not
identical nm storage categories: the later audit found late_time_init in BSS
instead of its requested .init.data; see pointer-declarator-section.out.
